{
  "id": 286330202,
  "iid": 14668,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "SMTP: Fix invalid password decoding",
  "description": "When the option _smtp.decryption_ is TRUE the SMTP disassembler fails _decrypting_ password.\n\nProblem lies in calling function _line_is_smtp_command()_ just after decoding the password (smtp auth_state is SMTP_AUTH_STATE_PASSWORD_REQ).\n\nCalling _line_is_smtp_command()_ returns TRUE when the cleartext password starts with 4 alphabetic ascii characters followed by a blank misleading the expected behaviour.\n\nWith this fix _line_is_smtp_command()_ is only used when smtp auth state is different to SMTP_AUTH_STATE_PASSWORD_REQ.\n\nIf _smtp.decryption_ option is disabled all is working as expected because the password is encoded in BASE64 (no blanks allowed), on the other hand if the cleartext password starts with more than 4 alphabetic ascii characters it will work but just by chance.\n\nFind attached a PCAP file that shows the issue: [smtp-test.pcap](/uploads/d3c2aee4bbbdde7244dea31ce67c6394/smtp-test.pcap)\n\nI can provide a TLS SMTP traffic with real data **but only privately** due to security reasons.\n\nPS: I'm using the term _decryption_ just because the name of the option includes it.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-03-04T15:20:17.081Z",
  "updated_at": "2024-03-05T20:58:54.104Z",
